# C conventions

## Comments

- Put a short comment above every function saying what it does and when it returns NULL / no-op.
- Comment non-obvious values: coordinate flips, reserved gutters, compile-time include guards, index offsets.
- Do not narrate the next line. Name the invariant.

```c
/* Icon row 0 is visual top; index() uses y=0 as the bottom LED. */
uint8_t y = (ROWS - 1) - (origin_y + row);
```

## KISS

- Ship the behavior asked for. Do not add caches, change-detection, or animation hooks “for later” unless they are required now.
- Prefer a table indexed by id over a long switch.
- Derive layout from sizes: `(COLS - ICON_W) / 2`, not a magic `2`.
- Do not bounds-check data this file owns (const bitmaps, enum tokens).

```c
/* ❌ BAD — cache + ready flags so pointers differ */
/* ✅ GOOD — one buffer, compose when that mode is active */
```

## DRY

- One function, `#if` inside, not two copies of the same symbol.
- Reuse existing module APIs (`bkpd_mode_get_active_id()`) instead of mirroring state.
- Keep pixel data in one translation unit. If a header is included from two `.c` files, do not put `static const` bitmaps in that header without a define guard — they will be duplicated in flash.

## Split

- Data structures and bitmaps: header (or one data `.c`).
- Logic: pick what to show (mode → icon).
- Display: blit / flush only.

## Style

- Match existing headers (copyright, SPDX, QMK include order).
- `static` unless another file needs the symbol.
